Thanks! Yes, if someone said they'd do something, it counts. Yes, turn vague deadlines into a date when the notes make it clear. The file name each time is fine. Format: a markdown memo, at most 400 words, with the action items as a table with columns Owner | Action | Due (ISO dates, 'none' if there's no date). The rest of your defaults are fine, the deliverables folder too. Please keep it cheap, but I need it right - about 12 runs per memo. And please use cheaper models: claude-sonnet-4.6 for the team lead and for whoever checks the memo, and claude-haiku-4.5 for everyone else.